-- Swamp of Sorrows C (_40): the doubled wildlife layer, retired leftovers and the second Midsummer copy (plan C-01..C-03;
-- S5 dossier 3 Parts A, B, D; generated by R\tmp\S5\gen.py, re-checked against mop_world 2026-11-17).
--
-- SOURCED: the TDB 12.1.0 sniff (the 4.4.2 box holds the same rows) and Wowhead MoP Classic map pins. Part A: per entry, spawns
-- closer than 15 yd to another of the same entry are one mob recorded twice (the TDB has 25 such pairs in 603, mop 375 in 1025);
-- a cluster keeps its members with a TDB partner within 40 yd, or one member if none has. Enthralled sea creatures in Stagalbog
-- Cave: one spawn per spot (two or three entries stacked). Part B: Watcher Biggs ends only retired quests and is in neither TDB;
-- Tok'Kar 5592 and Katar 5593 at Misty Reed Post stay (Wowhead MoP Classic pins them there, gate pages 2026-11-17, although
-- they too end only retired quests and the retail sniff has none); the level-39 Shadow Panther was the classic placeholder of Captain
-- Wyrmak's pool; five Pilgrim's Bounty Wild Turkeys stand on spirit-healer spots (no TDB turkey in the zone; Burning Steppes
-- deleted the same layer). Part D: 12 Midsummer rows at Bogpaddle are exact copies of the 352xxx rows.
-- OURS: the 15-yd / 40-yd thresholds of the rule (S5 section 1).
-- Every dependent row of a deleted spawn goes with it (addon, owned waypoint paths, pool, event, formation, linked respawn,
-- movement override, guid SmartAI). No entry of the Stonard battle (plan section 3, B) and no actor of section D is touched.
-- Ships with _43: deleting the Shadow Panther leaves pool 170 with Wyrmak alone at chance 12, which spawns nothing on 88 % of
-- rolls and never retries; _43 rebuilds pool 170.
-- Idempotent: DELETE.

